When I first encountered these issues, it was on an unreleased =
MontaVista x86 (32bit) distro, but I've confirmed it in Ubuntu 9.04 for =
ppoll01, mq_timedreceive01.=20

1. Specs are Core 2 Duo 2.13GHZ, 2GB memory.
2. config attached.
3. Ubuntu 9.04 (64 bit) on 2.6.28-13

LTP was compiled with a 32 bit i686-gnu toolchain.=20

I only bring these up as they have the potential to hang an LTP run, and =
are not consistent. Perhaps someone can more quickly spot the error in =
the test than I. I've haven't been able to to reproduce this on single =
core targets.

I was not able to reproduce ptrace06 hang except on a virtual target =
(vmware server)

